# G7 — THE GROUND A SCENARIO STANDS ON, AND THE STREAMER OVER IT.
#
# GROUND_DEFAULT's whole point in one script: say what untouched ground IS, and the
# world is that everywhere, without a cell being written.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS ALSO THE MEASUREMENT `G6` DEFERRED. Its streamer check was a code read —
# the loop sweeps a box around the CHARACTER and filters by hex distance, never asking
# whether a chunk exists — and demonstrating that at runtime needs a world with a
# ground actually set, which is this step. Walk somewhere nothing was ever written and
# the chunks still arrive.

# ⚠ NO `wait rebuilt` HERE. Nothing has been asked to change yet, so the event never
# comes and the wait runs its full 40 s into a discarded value — the same dead-wait
# shape STATE.md records costing 71 % of a gate.
echo --- a world with nothing in it
at 0 0 0

echo --- the ground is rock at 60, said once
ground 60 2
wait rebuilt

echo --- and the character walks far from anything anybody authored
at 240 -180 0
wait rebuilt

# ⚠ MEASURED 2026-08-12, and this is the row `G6` deferred:
#
#     editor: ground 60 material 2, 48 chunks to redraw
#     editor: rebuilt 48 chunks in 971 ms
#     editor: hex (139,-120) — +46 −48 chunks, 46 live
#
# 46 chunks ADDED at a hex where nothing was ever written. The streamer bounds by
# DISTANCE FROM THE CHARACTER, not by which chunks exist — a streamer that enumerated
# existing chunks would have added zero and the world would have looked empty.
